From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [fsdp] fix: all-reduce on the HSDP replicate group while the
 device memory is still free

An FSDP2 training engine on a 2D mesh all-reduces one element and a tensor of its largest unit's gradient shard
size on the replicate group right after sharding, before the optimizer is built. NCCL then sets up the group's
communicator and buffers there, not at the first update's all-reduce.
---
 ..._fsdp_gradient_accumulation_sync_on_cpu.py | 62 +++++++++++++++++++
 verl/workers/engine/fsdp/transformer_impl.py  | 28 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 90 insertions(+)

